From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TurboVadim <yolkin.vadim@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 17:59:04 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Cache waypoint connection snapshots

Reuse Guava entry-membership snapshots and player row views until a pair changes. Keep the original table, live entry values, iteration order and validation/send points, including reentrant sends. Identical block/chunk position objects have zero distance.

Packet differential coverage: 80,000 operations, reentrant updates, and 10,000 checks against the old connection arithmetic and packets.

Combined waypoint and no-listener movement changes, six interleaved players-moving runs per jar: 9.436 -> 7.058 ms/tick, -25.20% with a 95% half-width of 1.13 percentage points. Main-thread allocation: 9165.735 -> 5007.162 KiB/tick, -45.37% with a 95% half-width of 0.61 points. Exact digests match. All six other scenarios passed two runs per jar without digest drift or a significant performance difference. One optimized target run logged a pre-event movement-validation rejection whose physical cause was not reconstructed. All six original pairs are retained in the statistics and the warning is documented in the report.

